>> title: Takikomi Gohan
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: japanese, rice, chicken, shiitake, dashi, one pot
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: 炊き込みご飯, takikomi gohan, takikomi gohan, たきこみごはん, seasoned rice, Japanese mixed rice, rice cooked in dashi, kayaku gohan
>> pairs-with: dashi, tonjiru
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 5 min
>> slack: forgiving — it will sit on its rest for half an hour and reheats well the next day; what it will not survive is being stirred while it cooks, which breaks the grains and leaves the bottom as paste
>> step.1: rinse, then drain 30 min
>> step.2: stir the seasoning into the liquid
>> step.3: spread, pour over, lay on top
>> step.4: boil, then 12 min on the lowest heat
>> step.5: rest 10 min, then fold

Rinse @short-grain rice{2%cups}(475 mL, 370 g) in @cold water{6%cups}(1.4 L; poured off and replaced four or five times) ~rinse{3%min} until it runs almost clear, then leave it in a sieve to ~drain{30%min}, which is this recipe's version of a soak.

Stir @soy sauce{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @mirin{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @sake{1%Tbs}(15 mL) into @dashi{2%cups}(475 mL; or 2 cups water and 1 tsp dashi granules) in a #jug{}. The seasoning goes into the liquid and never onto the rice: soy poured on dry grains colours them in patches and they cook at different speeds.

Spread @&(1)drained rice{} in a #heavy saucepan{}, pour @&(~1)seasoned dashi{} over it, and lay @chicken thigh{5%oz}(150 g; boneless, in 1/2-inch dice), @dried shiitake{4}(soaked soft and sliced), @carrot{1/2}(in matchsticks) and @abura-age{1%sheet}(doused with boiling water to take the frying oil off, then sliced thin) on top without stirring any of it in.

Bring @&(~1)pot{} to a boil uncovered, then clamp the lid on and drop to the lowest flame ~steam{12%min}.

Rest @&(~1)rice{} off the heat with the lid shut ~rest{10%min}, then fold it over from the bottom of the pan so the seasoning that has sunk comes back up through it.
